# Vercel Speed Insights Installation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Saahvik HMS frontend application (React + Vite).

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added**: `@vercel/speed-insights` (v2.0.0) to dependencies
- **Updated**: `package.json` and `package-lock.json` with the new package

### 2. Code Integration
- **Modified**: `frontend/src/main.tsx`
  - Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/react"`
  - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component to the render tree, placed alongside the existing `<Analytics />` component

## Implementation Details

### Installation Method
Followed the latest official Vercel Speed Insights documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart:
- Installed the package using npm
- Imported the React-specific SpeedInsights component
- Added the component at the root level of the application

### Placement Strategy
The `<SpeedInsights />` component was added in the main.tsx file within the component tree:
```tsx
<QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>
  <AuthProvider>
    <ToastProvider>
      <RouterProvider router={router} />
      <Analytics />
      <SpeedInsights />  // <-- Added here
    </ToastProvider>
  </AuthProvider>
</QueryClientProvider>
```

This placement ensures:
- Speed Insights tracks all routes and page transitions
- It's initialized early in the component tree
- It follows the same pattern as the existing Analytics component
- The component is rendered once at the application root level

## Verification

### Build Verification
- ✅ TypeScript compilation successful (tsc -b)
- ✅ Vite build completed successfully
- ✅ No errors or warnings introduced
- ✅ Build output sizes are normal

### Files Changed
1. `frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
2. `frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated lockfile with new package and dependencies
3. `frontend/src/main.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights import and component

## Next Steps

To complete the Speed Insights setup:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard:
   - Navigate to your project settings
   - Go to Speed Insights in the sidebar
   - Click the "Enable" button
3. After deployment and user visits, performance metrics will appear in the Vercel dashboard

## Notes
- The Speed Insights component automatically tracks Core Web Vitals and other performance metrics
- No additional configuration is required for basic usage
- The component is framework-aware and optimized for React applications
- Metrics will only be collected when deployed on Vercel's platform
